                <pb facs="0112" n="30" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg30"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 611.3231/185.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-01-02"><hi rendition="#italic">January 2,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Executive is authorized to grant during 1911, 30 per cent reduction in the
                    duty on flour and 20 per cent on one or more other articles of American
                    production.</p>
                <p>Parcel post and arbitration conventions with the United States ratified by
                    Congress December 30. Exchange of the ratifications of the former here
                    awaited.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dudley.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
